</section><section id="activity-6"><h1 id="activity-6-h">Activity 6<span class="kicker">Proposed assessment strategy</span></h1>
<div class="card"><p><strong>Proposed Assessment Strategy</strong></p>
<p><strong>Unit cluster:</strong> Please see <a href="#unit-cluster">"Unit cluster"</a> section.</p>
<p><strong>Purpose and design decisions</strong></p>
<p>This proposed strategy is for the future delivery of the two
clustered units over 9 weeks. It builds on the <strong>existing</strong>
Lopez Law quiz and project but <strong>introduces changes</strong> to
address gaps identified in my critical evaluation (i.e., OLTC20002:
Assessment Task 1). The design is guided by the Assessment Design
Decisions Framework (Bearman et al., 2014), the ASQA Principles of
Assessment and Rules of Evidence (ASQA, 2025), and the requirements of
both units (Training.gov.au, n.d.-a, n.d.-b).</p>
<div class="tablewrap"><table>

<thead>
<tr class="header">
<th><strong>Area</strong></th>
<th><strong>Proposed decision</strong></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr class="odd">
<td>Purpose</td>
<td>Certify competence (i.e., Satisfactory / Not Satisfactory (S/NS))
while supporting learning through practice and staged feedback.</td>
</tr>
<tr class="even">
<td>Context</td>
<td>Small mixed-mode classes, Weekly Zoom and two labs, CQU and ASQA
requirements.</td>
</tr>
<tr class="odd">
<td>Evidence</td>
<td>Quiz for knowledge evidence and a simulated workplace staged project
for performance evidence.</td>
</tr>
<tr class="even">
<td>Feedback</td>
<td>Weekly practice and feedback/client sign-off after each project
stage. The unit coordinator will play the role of the client.</td>
</tr>
<tr class="odd">
<td>Learner outcomes</td>
<td>Both tasks together will cover all knowledge and performance
evidence of both units. Please refer to the “Mapping to Unit
Requirements” section below.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p><strong>Task 1: Small Business Networking Quiz</strong></p>
<div class="tablewrap"><table>

<thead>
<tr class="header">
<th><strong>Item</strong></th>
<th><strong>Proposed approach</strong></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr class="odd">
<td>Result / timing</td>
<td>S/NS. 100% result required. Opens in Week 1. Due Thursday of Week
9.</td>
</tr>
<tr class="even">
<td>Format</td>
<td>18-question individual, open-book Moodle quiz, five attempts with a
one-hour study break after unsuccessful attempts.</td>
</tr>
<tr class="odd">
<td>Coverage</td>
<td>SOHO Network requirements, standards, devices/services. TCP/IP,
network types, installation, Security, testing/diagnosis and media.</td>
</tr>
<tr class="even">
<td>Changes</td>
<td><strong>Add Q18 on OSI layers/functions</strong>. Change Q15-Q16 to
teacher-marked short answers requiring students to explain a fault and
corrective action.</td>
</tr>
<tr class="odd">
<td>Conditions</td>
<td>Own work. Short answers must be in the student's own words and
completed without GenAI.</td>
</tr>
<tr class="even">
<td>Assessor decision</td>
<td>Auto-marked in Moodle. Q15–Q16 teacher-marked against a model
answer. Satisfactory when all 18 questions are correct.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p><em><strong>Rationale</strong></em>: Open-book assessment reflects
workplace practice, while 100% accuracy maintains the required standard.
Multiple attempts can support learning through feedback (Boud &amp;
Associates, 2010). The added OSI question and revised fault questions
strengthen evidence of ICTNWK311 knowledge and troubleshooting.</p>
<p><strong>Task 2: SOHO Network Project</strong></p>
<p>Students complete an individual four-stage Lopez Law project to
design and configure a network for a small law firm, including
PCs/mobile devices, NAS, VoIP, printer, VPN, NBN, WiFi extender and
camera. The teacher acts as the client. Each stage requires satisfactory
sign-off before progressing, with three attempts available. The project
is Satisfactory when all four stages and observation checklist items are
completed.</p>
<div class="tablewrap"><table>

<thead>
<tr class="header">
<th><strong>Stage</strong></th>
<th><strong>Proposed activity and evidence</strong></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr class="odd">
<td>1. Research (Week 3)</td>
<td>Clarify requirements, research equipment, cabling, NBN and costs.
Draw a logical diagram. <em><strong><u>New</u></strong></em>: justify
each recommendation against a client requirement.
<em><strong>Evidence</strong></em>: purchasing document and oral
sign-off.</td>
</tr>
<tr class="even">
<td>2. Proposal (Week 5)</td>
<td>Prepare IP/naming, WiFi, sharing, security and task sequence.
<em><strong><u>New</u></strong></em>: include a test plan using ping,
ipconfig, nslookup and tracert with expected results.
<em><strong>Evidence</strong></em>: network plan.</td>
</tr>
<tr class="odd">
<td>3. Implementation (Weeks 6-8)</td>
<td>Build and demonstrate the pilot network.
<em><strong><u>New</u></strong></em>: record tests, diagnose and fix a
teacher-introduced fault, and answer 'explain your work' questions.
<em><strong>Evidence</strong></em>: updated observation checklist.</td>
</tr>
<tr class="even">
<td>4. Documentation (Thursday, Week 9)</td>
<td>Update the plan and configuration screenshots.
<em><strong><u>New</u></strong></em>: include test results and a
troubleshooting log. <em><strong>Evidence</strong></em>: final network
documentation.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p><em><strong>Conditions</strong></em>: individual work - Stage 3 is
supervised after the safety induction. GenAI may support learning, but
submitted content must be in the student's own words. A realistic
requirements-to-documentation workflow supports authenticity and job
readiness (Race, 2015). Staged feedback supports improvement before
final judgement (Boud &amp; Associates, 2010), while direct observation,
testing, troubleshooting and questioning strengthen authenticity and
reliability of evidence (ASQA, 2025).</p>
<p><strong>Mapping to unit requirements</strong></p>
<p>The proposed changes are intended to close the previously identified
gaps (OLTC20002: Assessment Task 1). The full unit requirements remain
those published on Training.gov.au (n.d.-a, n.d.-b).</p>
<div class="tablewrap"><table style="width:100%;">

<thead>
